{% if "open_port_database" in data.contains_type %}
    <li>{% trans %}The following servers have open database ports:{% endtrans %}
        <ul>
            {% for report in data.reports %}
                {% if report.report_type == "open_port_database" %}
                    <li>
                        {{ report.target }} ({{ report.additional_data.service }})
                        {{ report_meta(report) }}
                    </li>
                {% endif %}
            {% endfor %}
        </ul>
        <p>
            {% trans trimmed %}
                This is not a vulnerability and does not mean that anyone can log in to the database - logging in still
                requires a username and password. Blocking external access to the database provides an additional layer of
                security - for example, if a backup of a configuration file containing the password is accidentally made
                public, or if a vulnerability in the application is exploited to read files. Keeping the database port from
                being publicly accessible makes it significantly harder for attackers to continue an attack.
            {% endtrans %}
        </p>
    </li>
{% endif %}
